# awesome-parenting-gear

Baby & kids gear that actually works, picked by a dad of 3.
Prices in CHF (indicative, September 2026). Sources: ADAC, TCS, BPA, Stiftung Warentest.
No affiliate links, no sponsorship.

> ⚠️ Always check the seat manufacturer's vehicle compatibility list and try car seats in store before buying.

---

## 🚗 Car seats

**Best plan: 2 steps, one shared rotating base.**

| Stage | Product | Size | ADAC | Price |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–15 months | Cybex Cloud T + Base T | 40–87 cm | – | ~350 CHF |
| Then | **Cybex Sirona T i-Size** (on same Base T) | 45–105 cm | 2.3 (2023) | ~350 CHF |
| Then | **Britax Römer Kidfix Pro** (booster) | 100–150 cm | 1.8 | ~250 CHF |
| or | Cybex Solution G2 (booster) | 100–150 cm | 2.1 | ~200 CHF |

**Alternatives (rotating)**

| Product | Size | ADAC | Price |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cybex Sirona Ti | 40–105 cm | 2.5 (2026) | ~550 CHF |
| Avionaut Stardust (rear-facing up to 125 cm) | 40–150 cm | 3.3 (2026) | ~550 CHF |
| Maxi-Cosi Emerald 360 Pro (one seat for everything) | 40–150 cm | 3.1 (2026) | ~500 CHF |

**Avoid:** Chipolino Olympus, Reecle 360, Lionelo Lavender, cheap no-name "0–12 years 360°" seats.

**Rules (Switzerland):** approved seat mandatory until 12 years or 150 cm. Rear-facing mandatory until at least 76 cm and 15 months (R129). Keep rear-facing as long as possible (BPA). Replace any seat after an accident.

